I left out both of the operations requests. This node's only granted capability is `StateHandle<'subscriptions', read>`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP import. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond its declared contract. The metadata call would also send the raw input text to an external host, which the contract doesn't permit. If operations needs logging or enrichment, that should be a separate node with its own declared capabilities, reviewed as such.

The state key `"urls"` and the newline-separated value format are my assumptions. Adjust them to match the store's actual contents. If no usable URLs are found, the node traps rather than return a list that violates `present(urls)`.

